```
# ============================================================================
# Detection: Network/Host Discovery Sweep from Single Source
# Detection ID: DE-DI-002
# MITRE ATT&CK: T1018 - Remote System Discovery / T1046 - Network Service Discovery
# Data Source: Firewall/NetFlow logs
# Severity: Low
# ============================================================================

index=network sourcetype=firewall action=allowed
| bucket _time span=5m
| stats dc(dest_ip) as unique_hosts_contacted dc(dest_port) as unique_ports values(dest_port) as ports by src_ip, _time
| where unique_hosts_contacted>=20 OR unique_ports>=15
| sort -unique_hosts_contacted
```

## Detection Logic
Flags a single internal source contacting an unusually high number of distinct internal hosts or ports in a tight window — consistent with nmap/masscan-style network sweeps or tools like SharpHound/BloodHound performing SMB/LDAP discovery against many endpoints.

## False Positive Considerations
Vulnerability scanners (Nessus/Qualys/Rapid7) and asset-management tools do this by design — allowlist their scanner service IPs, this is a mandatory exclusion for this detection to be usable.

## Tuning Notes
Feed to SOC dashboard as a contextual/enrichment panel; combine with T1087 discovery hits from the same host/user for a stronger recon-chain narrative.
